  calling you an imbecile in spanish you  definitely should get into resident evil  4 and vr on metaquest 2. the story  immediately immerses you i'm under the  president's order to rescue you so it's  easy to get into the role of a special  agent trying to save the president's  daughter the gameplay is fun and  challenging with a creepy retro feeling  art style that increases the anxiety and  tension you feel as you push open each  door using your actual hands resident  evil 4 was never the most terrifying  game in the series but adding the  immersion of the first person vr makes  it so much scarier you can almost feel  the wind from the gonados axes as they  whizz past your head and you never  realize just how huge your gigantes  actually are until you have to crane  your neck to see their eyes as you stand  toed a giant toe with one the metaquest  ii's high per-eye resolution really  helps see the gross details that  armature painstakingly repainted and  uprest to bring the original re4 assets  into a 360 degree world and the audio  has been reworked to create a 3d spatial  soundscape that makes you whip your head  around and panic at every creaky board  but that instinct will keep you alive as  the infected will make noise from the  direction they are attacking from  armature built the game around the  original building blocks of re4 trying  to preserve as much of the gameplay  style and feel as possible while  upgrading the game to vr the story is  the same the cut scenes are in their  original format character animations  have stayed the same other than being  converted to the latest unreal engine  and altered to be experienced from vr  the world itself is based on the exact  same geometry as the original version  meaning those little tricks you use to  outsmart the gennados might still work  exactly like they used to the quicktime  events have been updated to work with  the metaquest touch controllers so  instead of pressing a sequence of  buttons you'll need 